%I A244524 #24 Nov 08 2026 23:14:39
%S A244524 1,1,4,26,236,2780,40642,715836,14873174,358866952,9934283924,
%T A244524 312461402424,11076935794874,439555827441468
%N A244524 Number of pairs (f,g) of commuting maps {0,..,n-1}->{0,..,n-1} with 0 <= f(k), g(k) <= k.
%F A244524 For n >= 1, let F_n be the set of maps f: {0,...,n-1} -> {0,...,n-1} satisfying f(i) <= i. For f in F_n, define D_i(t), 0 <= t <= i, recursively for i = n-1,...,0 by
%F A244524 D_i(t) = Product_{j>i, f(j)=i} (Sum_{0<=u<=j, f(u)=t} D_j(u)).
%F A244524 Then
%F A244524 a(n) = Sum_{f in F_n} Product_{r: f(r)=r} (Sum_{0<=t<=r, f(t)=t} D_r(t)),
%F A244524 where empty products equal 1. Also a(0) = 1. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Nov 08 2026
%e A244524 The a(3) = 26 pairs of such maps are (dots for zeros in the maps):
%e A244524 01:  [ . . . ]  [ . . . ]
%e A244524 02:  [ . . . ]  [ . . 1 ]
%e A244524 03:  [ . . . ]  [ . . 2 ]
%e A244524 04:  [ . . . ]  [ . 1 . ]
%e A244524 05:  [ . . . ]  [ . 1 1 ]
%e A244524 06:  [ . . . ]  [ . 1 2 ]
%e A244524 07:  [ . . 1 ]  [ . . . ]
%e A244524 08:  [ . . 1 ]  [ . . 1 ]
%e A244524 09:  [ . . 1 ]  [ . 1 2 ]
%e A244524 10:  [ . . 2 ]  [ . . . ]
